====================================================================================================
 MarXus master equation
====================================================================================================
 RUN SETTINGS
 ------------
 Deck:               /tmp/tmp.isq3cCKP0W/c2h3_shock_incubation_de0.1.inp
 Method:             DIRECT TIME INTEGRATION of the grained populations, dN/dt = R F - J N, and of the yields of every exit
                     initial state: initial population and sources of the Preparation block (Source, below)
                     output times 1e-12 .. 1e-3 s, 8 per decade (operator of the final steady state)
 Solvers:            adaptive L-stable Rosenbrock method Rodas4 (adapted from KPP; Hairer, Wanner, Solving ODEs II, Sec. IV.7)
                     relative tolerance 1e-8, absolute 1e-14; steps of powers of two, banded Cholesky of s I + S reused
 Parallel:           8 cores (--ncore); the 1 conditions (T, p) in batches of 1 at a time (rayon)
                     BLAS threads per LAPACK call: 8
 Temperatures (K):   1000
 Pressures (torr):   760
 Energy grid:        grains of 70.000 cm-1 on a common absolute scale, sums of 1 cm-1 counting cells
 Collisions:         exponential down, exactly normalized (Robertson (ed.), CCK 43 (2019), eq. 4.16), transitions up to 15 <dE_down>
                     low-energy reservoirs where eq. 4.16 fails (sparse states, Robertson 2019, p. 294): the grains from the
                       failing one down form one thermalized state (reservoir state, MESMER manual, Sec. 14.2.1):
                       T = 1000 K: W1 1 grains (70 cm-1, 19.4 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                     collision frequency: Lennard-Jones (per well, below); collision integral Omega(2,2)*: Neufeld, Janzen, Aziz, J. Chem. Phys. 57, 1100 (1972) (default)
 Tunneling:          exact Eckart transmission (Miller, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 101, 6810 (1979), eq. 8)
 Source:             prepared experiment (Preparation block of the deck; reports/nonthermal_sources_design.md)
                     initial population given
                     bath: every condition of the deck
====================================================================================================
 CHEMICAL NETWORK
 ----------------

Wells (collisions: <dE_down>(T) = <dE_down>(T_ref) (T/T_ref)^n; Lennard-Jones collision frequency):
      Name   grains    absolute grains   collisions; sink
        W1     2172       -172 .. 1999   <dE_down> = 200 cm-1 (T/300 K)^0.85; sigma 3.455 A, epsilon 64.82 K, reduced mass 3.797 amu

Channels (k(E) of every channel; rate model from the deck):
      Name     From       To   Model
        B1       W1       P1   rigid transition state; entrance of the reactant (source)

Energetics (kcal/mol, relative to P1):

Wells (G - ground energy, D - lowest barrier out of the well):
      Name          G          D
        W1     -34.44       4.42

Bimolecular (G - ground energy):
      Name          G
        P1       0.00

Barriers (H - ZeroEnergy of the barrier in the deck):
      Name          H     From       To   Model
        B1       4.42       W1       P1   rigid transition state

====================================================================================================
 PARTITION FUNCTIONS AND EQUILIBRIUM CONSTANTS
 ---------------------------------------------

From the cell densities of states of the master equation (the counting of k(E)); tight barriers included, phase-space-theory and ILT barriers have no RRHO partition function.

Temperature = 1000 K

Partition functions (Q from the ground state of the species; bimolecular species per cm^3, with the relative translation; E0: ground energy in kcal/mol on the energy scale of the deck):
      Name         Kind           E0             Q
        W1         well     -34.4400   1.18489e+05
        B1      barrier       4.4200   4.26676e+05
        P1  bimolecular       0.0000   2.49761e+28

Real equilibrium constants Q_X exp(-E_X/kT) / (Q_Y exp(-E_Y/kT)), rows X, columns Y (bimolecular units cm^3):
Q/Q             W1           P1
W1     1.00000e+00  1.59540e-16
P1     6.26800e+15  1.00000e+00

====================================================================================================
Units: unimolecular rate coefficients 1/s; bimolecular rate coefficients cm^3/s; yields in %.
Numbers with six significant digits; *** marks a value that is not available.
====================================================================================================

____________________________________________________________________________________________________
PREPARED EXPERIMENT: DIRECT TIME INTEGRATION
____________________________________________________________________________________________________

dn/dt = -J[T_b(t), p(t)] n + sum_a R_a(t) F_a with n(0) = N_0 F_0, and dY_x/dt = k_x^T n: the initial population and
the source channels of the Preparation block, with impulses as exact jumps and the bath segments as events
(reports/nonthermal_sources_design.md). Populations and yields in the units of the given amounts.

